 "problems": [
  "Cliopatria row people-s-republic-of-zanzibar (1856-1889) is the Sultanate of Zanzibar; its Wikipedia title and Wikidata Q157535 are the 1964 republic's. sultanate-of-zanzibar (1963-1966, af-08) is the same sultanate: link or merge.",
  "Cliopatria row omani-slave-coast (1814-1855) is the Omani Empire's African dominion; its 1840-1855 shape reaches 14.6 S and Cape Guardafui, which the Omani Empire page does not support; the African coast is inside the sultanate-of-oman shapes 1744-1814.",
  "Many Wikipedia pages for the Great Lakes kingdoms are thin on dated territory: placeholder years at confidence 1 (Kilwa dependencies 1400, Buganda 1300 and 1800, Bunyoro 1590/1800/1830, Rwanda 1881, Unyanyembe 1800) and single full-extent keyframes for Ankole, Rwanda, Burundi.",
  "Page budget for people-s-republic-of-zanzibar (1-2) was exceeded (six pages) because the 1885-1890 events are on pages the German and British gains also need.",
  "No tool failures; WebFetch refused only three nonexistent titles (listed in pages_failed). Counterpart slugs not yet backed by a dossier at the time of writing: german-africa (af-08), sultanate-of-oman (me-10), british-colonial-empire (eu-11) exist as polities; sultanate-of-the-geledi, sultanate-of-malindi, uganda-protectorate and east-africa-protectorate do not."
 ]
}